a beloved staple in our community was  completely destroyed in a fire yesterday  the mount charleston lodge is set to be  a total loss the blaze started before  sunrise and took crews from both the  mount charleston and clark county fire  departments to put it out luckily no one  was hurt and dozens of employees at the  mount charleston lodge are mourning  after that loss and yesterday's  devastating fire but they are also now  without a job now the resort just down  the mountain is hosting a job fair for  them victoria saha joins us from mount  charleston as the mountain community  picks up the pieces  the small community here on mount  charleston is slowly rebuilding the  employees over at the lodge don't have  to worry about being without a job any  longer because the resort here on mount  charleston is opening their doors to  them  owner of the resort on mount charleston  deanna crossman flew in saturday morning  to help her neighbors at the lodge any  way she can we just want to work  together you know we're stronger  together she knew the significance the  lodge had on the mountain and employees  who now have nowhere to go  a lot of people work up here because  they don't want to work in the valley  right and it's just different and we're  the only other option and we  with being the only place left we want  to just make sure people had a home up  here if they  they wanted to stay on saturday she  hosted a job fair for those displaced  employees emily was one of them and now  she'll be working at the resort  always amazing every time i come in here  and the restaurant was the same way it's  always a very welcoming environment and  it's so lovely that they would do  something like that for us the owner of  this resort says she's ok being a  temporary home for the displaced  employees until the lodge is rebuilt  again reporting from mount charleston  victoria saha live local now
 

